### Interaction with the PR nudge and NudgeLimit

`Problems` still contains "a failed check", so gone-worker relaunch and the idle state chaser keep working unchanged. Order on an idle In Review ticket: comment nudge, then `inReviewIdle`'s ready notify, then escalation if `Nudges >= NudgeLimit`, then the CI forward, then the PR nudge. `watch` calls `ciNudge` before the worker switch; its guard above hands the tick to `inReviewIdle` when escalation is due. One action per ticket per tick holds, so the forward replaces the PR nudge that tick.

The forward on an idle In Review worker counts as a nudge (`CountsAsPRNudge`, executed as `e.Nudges++`). It is a message about this PR to an idle worker, and counting it keeps the escalation budget honest: forward (1), PR nudge on a later tick (2), then Escalate. Without counting, an idle worker would get three messages about one failure before escalation. For Working workers and In Progress tickets the forward is not counted, as with the comment nudge, because counting would make a busy worker look idle-through-N-nudges and escalate wrongly.

I do not suppress "a failed check" in the PR nudge once forwarded: that would remove the only escalation path for an idle worker that ignores the forward.

